ence over time\"}]}], \"methods_quotes\": [{\"loc\": \"text\", \"q\": \"All analyses were conducted using statistical software to account for the complex sampling design and to calculate prevalence estimates and 95% confidence intervals (CIs).\"}, {\"loc\": \"text\", \"q\": \"derived from Current Population Surveys, based on weighted, unstandardized prevalence estimates\"}, {\"loc\": \"note\", \"q\": \"Weighted prevalence estimates, directly standardized to the 2000 U.S. standard population, based on the following age groups: 20--39, 40--59, and ≥60 years.\"}, {\"loc\": \"note\", \"q\": \"Linear trend in prevalence shows significant decline (p<0.01) from 1999--2000 to 2007--2008 after adjustment for sex, age group, race/ethnicity, and poverty-income ratio.\"}], \"confidence\": \"high\", \"uncertain_fields\": [\"outcome_types\"]}", "type": "text"}]}